# The "New" hints next to Manufacturer and Part in the car dialog have to go
# once the fields name a part that exists (Development Issues #77, Ken's
# steps): add car Ken/ken1, start a second car, change the manufacturer to
# Ken2 and back to Ken with part ken1 again. FOCUSOUT is the entry losing
# focus, which is when the dialog decides a typed name is new.
# Adding the first car also checks that a car added during playback is
# kept: the custom-file save, which playback skips, used to undo it.
VERSION 13
DEMOINIT
ORIG 0.000 0.000 0.000
ROOMSIZE 40.000 x 20.000
SCALE HO
REDRAW
PARAMETER misc cmdCarInventory
PARAMETER carinv add
PARAMETER carpart manuf -1 Ken
PARAMETER carpart manuf FOCUSOUT
PARAMETER carpart partno-list -1 ken1
PARAMETER carpart partno-list FOCUSOUT
PARAMETER carpart desc ken1 desc
PARAMCHECK carpart manuf-new shown
PARAMCHECK carpart partno-new shown
PARAMETER carpart ok
PARAMETER carinv add
# The first car was added, so the index moved on.
PARAMCHECK carpart index 2
PARAMETER carpart manuf -1 Ken2
PARAMETER carpart manuf FOCUSOUT
PARAMCHECK carpart manuf-new shown
PARAMETER carpart partno-list -1 ken1
PARAMETER carpart partno-list FOCUSOUT
PARAMETER carpart desc ken1 desc
PARAMETER carpart manuf -1 Ken
PARAMETER carpart manuf FOCUSOUT
PARAMCHECK carpart manuf-new hidden
PARAMCHECK carpart partno-new hidden
# The dialog is back on the existing part, so Ok adds a second car of it
# without asking whether to update the part (no NOTICE in the log).
PARAMETER carpart ok
PARAMETER carinv add
PARAMCHECK carpart index 3
PARAMETER carpart cancel
PARAMETER carinv ok
